  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 300 AM EDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nNot much change in the extended periods. The models are generally\nin good agreement through the weekend. Troughing over the \nSoutheast for the end of the work week with ridging building into \nthe weekend.\n\nBeginning Wed afternoon/evening, under the influence of the \ntrough, chance to likely PoPs will prevail across the area through\nFriday. A few waves within the trough may diurnally enhance \nconvection each afternoon and lead to the potential for some \nisolated strong to severe storms. The models are showing a \nboundary developing over GA Wed night/Thu morning as a first main \nwave moves SE out of the Mid MS river valley and into W GA. This \nboundary stays nearly stationary through Friday so we could see a \nfairly active Thu/Fri. Precipitable water values near the boundary\nstay around the 2\" range beginning late Wed through Sat. This is \nmost likely why WPC has placed a good portions of the state under \na marginal risk of excessive rainfall for days 4 and 5. Would not \nbe surprised if SPC put us under a Marginal risk for severe storms\nas we get closer to Thu/Fri. Will need to see how the models \nhandle things over the next few runs to keep and eye on \nsevere/excessive rain trends.\n\nMoisture is forecasted to remain plentiful through the weekend, \nbut the Bermuda ridge is expected to begin to push back in across \nthe SERN U.S. This should help to cap the stronger to severe \ngrowth aspect of diurnal convective development Sat/Sun.",
